%% DM26-0670

%% The broker shuts down in order, as built (2026-11-04, docs/architecture/cassini-broker.md, infra/cassini-shutdown.nu). Asked over the wire with
%% its token, or by its own infrastructure when its pod is told to stop. Five phases, each with its own timeout, which forces it on.
sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    participant Op as operator (cassini-shutdown.nu),<br/>or the infrastructure's PrepareShutdown
    participant Broker
    participant Control as ControlManager
    participant LM as ListenerManager
    participant SM as SessionManager
    participant SA as SessionAgents
    participant TM as TopicManager
    participant Subs as SubscriberManager
    participant L as Listeners

    Op->>Broker: PrepareForShutdown(token)
    Broker->>Control: PrepareForShutdown(token)
    alt the token is not the one it started with (compared in constant time)
        Control->>Control: logged, and nothing happens
    else
        Note over Control: Phase by phase: each is asked for through the Broker, its completion comes back the same way,<br/>and a phase past its timeout has its manager stopped so that the next can begin.
        rect rgb(250, 240, 215)
        Note over Broker,LM: 1. StopAcceptingNewConnections
        Control->>LM: InitiateShutdownPhase, through the Broker
        LM->>LM: end the accept loop
        LM-->>Control: ShutdownPhaseComplete
        end
        rect rgb(250, 240, 215)
        Note over Broker,SA: 2. DrainExistingSessions
        Control->>SM: InitiateShutdownPhase, through the Broker
        SM->>SA: PrepareForShutdown: from now each publish is refused for now,<br/>which a client keeps for the broker that comes back
        Note over SM: A registration asked for now is refused ("Broker is shutting down").
        alt nothing pending
            SM->>SA: stop every session
        else publishes pending
            SA-->>SM: each answered publish lowers the count, and a session ends when it is done
        end
        SM-->>Control: ShutdownPhaseComplete, then the manager stops
        end
        rect rgb(250, 240, 215)
        Note over Broker,TM: 3. FlushTopicQueues
        Control->>TM: InitiateShutdownPhase, through the Broker
        TM->>TM: each topic pumps what waits, ignoring any hold,<br/>and the agents stop
        TM-->>Control: ShutdownPhaseComplete, then the manager stops
        end
        rect rgb(250, 240, 215)
        Note over Broker,Subs: 4. TerminateSubscribers
        Control->>Subs: InitiateShutdownPhase, through the Broker
        Subs->>Subs: each subscriber told and stopped, and what it holds is not flushed
        Subs-->>Control: ShutdownPhaseComplete
        end
        rect rgb(250, 240, 215)
        Note over Broker,L: 5. TerminateListeners
        Control->>LM: InitiateShutdownPhase, through the Broker
        LM->>L: stop each, and its connection closes
        LM-->>Control: ShutdownPhaseComplete, then the manager stops
        end
        Control->>Control: shutdown_completed, and it stops
        Note over Broker: The pressure manager ends with the drain. A client finds its connection gone,<br/>and its facade keeps its outbox and tries again until a broker is back.
    end
